/**
 * Armed-mode state machine. Only ever constructed by {@link FlashbackAutoMod} when the studio armed this launch.
 *
 * <p>Threads: a daemon watchdog thread (sleeps 200 ms) does everything that must not depend on the render thread
 * (STOP file, watchdog, stall detection, status.json, forced halt) and posts one {@link #step()} at a time to the
 * render thread. Flashback runs {@code ExportJob.run()} synchronously on the render thread, so while a shot renders
 * no step can run; the watchdog thread reads the job's public progress counters instead.
 *
 * <p>Minecraft is touched only through Flashback's public API plus a few intermediary names:
 * class_310 (Minecraft): method_1551 getInstance, field_1687 level, field_1724 player, field_1755 screen,
 * method_18506 overlay, method_1592 stop(), method_18854 isSameThread, execute(Runnable); class_442 TitleScreen;
